cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Runopsy: Causal Failure Analysis and Controlled Replay for AI Agent Runs"
message: "If you use Runopsy in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Runopsy is a local-first, open-source coding-agent CLI with a built-in causal
  failure analysis engine. It records agent runs as a normalized trace graph,
  localizes the suspected failure onset with linked evidence, measures downstream
  propagation, and supports user-approved replay from a checkpoint or session
  fork. Structural and behavioral analysis is deterministic and spends no model
  tokens; semantic analysis is optional and budget-bounded. Causal language is
  calibrated: a cause is stated as established only when a counterfactual replay
  or human verification supports it.
